## Appended 2026-09-12

`corpus_2026-09-12` supersedes `corpus_2026-09-11c`. It was regenerated at the
author's request with seed 42, and with the component overlap range widened so
the achieved overlap distribution matches the empirical one through its body.
10,000 datasets plus a 50-dataset probe set, 0 failed parents, 0 rejected.

NOTE: `data/processed/CORPUS.json` is a POINTER to the active corpus and
changes whenever the active corpus changes. Its row above pinned the value it
held on 2026-09-11 and is expected to fail after any switch. It should not have
been pinned; the rows that matter are the corpus artifacts themselves.

KNOWN DEFECT in this corpus, written up in reports/HANDOFF_stage-2a.md under
"START HERE": a third to a half of the multimodal datasets are unrealistic
spikes, because component separation is controlled by the AVERAGE pairwise
overlap, which barely constrains the modes that actually touch once there are
more than two. Do not use this corpus for analysis until that is settled.

